WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.139 --> 00:00:04.440
And then we've got some of the other bits of functionality.

2
00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:08.140
So what we've covered so far is the various ways

3
00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:11.220
that data can boil through.

4
00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:14.380
But once we're working within code,

5
00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:16.780
understanding things about our network environment

6
00:00:16.780 --> 00:00:19.460
can become quite important.

7
00:00:19.460 --> 00:00:21.179
So this isn't so much about dormancy.

8
00:00:21.179 --> 00:00:23.620
This is more about when you're writing your code,

9
00:00:23.620 --> 00:00:26.699
when you're writing, whether or not something is replicated,

10
00:00:26.699 --> 00:00:28.500
knowing whether you're on the server,

11
00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:31.140
whether you're on a client, what your current configuration

12
00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:33.740
state is becomes quite important.

13
00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:35.740
And that's where things like net mode come in.

14
00:00:35.740 --> 00:00:38.100
So net mode, again, this is probably

15
00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:41.899
more of an unreal bespoke specific end of things.

16
00:00:41.899 --> 00:00:47.280
But it may have a corollary on other proprietary software

17
00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:49.140
that you've worked with.

18
00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:52.820
But essentially, net mode is the most airtight,

19
00:00:52.820 --> 00:00:57.140
watertight way of checking what your current state is.

20
00:00:57.140 --> 00:00:59.060
We've talked in previous sessions

21
00:00:59.060 --> 00:01:04.099
about the idea of using with client code pragmas,

22
00:01:04.099 --> 00:01:05.739
with server code pragmas.

23
00:01:05.739 --> 00:01:09.000
But we've also talked about the fact that in editor,

24
00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:11.900
on standalone, both of those things will be true.

25
00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:14.599
So we can't always trust code that we write within those

26
00:01:14.599 --> 00:01:16.459
pragmas to only be suitable for the client

27
00:01:16.459 --> 00:01:18.459
or only be suitable for the server.

28
00:01:18.459 --> 00:01:21.340
And so that's where net mode comes in.

29
00:01:21.340 --> 00:01:24.659
Net mode can essentially have four states.

30
00:01:24.659 --> 00:01:27.099
It can be standalone, dedicated server,

31
00:01:27.140 --> 00:01:29.739
listen server or client.

32
00:01:29.739 --> 00:01:31.900
So standalone, I think we've talked

33
00:01:31.900 --> 00:01:34.379
about this configuration in our first session.

34
00:01:34.379 --> 00:01:39.939
But essentially, this is running in total isolation.

35
00:01:39.939 --> 00:01:42.980
So we never have to worry about a server coming in

36
00:01:42.980 --> 00:01:44.299
and writing into our data.

37
00:01:44.299 --> 00:01:47.219
We never have to worry about sending our data elsewhere.

38
00:01:47.219 --> 00:01:49.140
This is kind of a local build of our game.

39
00:01:49.140 --> 00:01:52.140
So if we have a game that is somehow

40
00:01:52.140 --> 00:01:55.099
both single-player and multiplayer,

41
00:01:55.140 --> 00:01:57.260
maybe that would be the situation you're in here.

42
00:01:57.260 --> 00:01:58.579
You might be in standalone.

43
00:01:58.579 --> 00:01:59.900
But for the most part, if you're making

44
00:01:59.900 --> 00:02:02.859
a single-player game and you queried your net mode

45
00:02:02.859 --> 00:02:04.219
of any of your actors,

46
00:02:04.219 --> 00:02:06.879
their net mode would be standalone.

47
00:02:06.879 --> 00:02:09.120
Dedicated server is the kind of opposite.

48
00:02:09.120 --> 00:02:11.759
It's where nothing in the game is being played.

49
00:02:12.840 --> 00:02:14.319
We already talked about the kind of role

50
00:02:14.319 --> 00:02:15.639
of a dedicated server.

51
00:02:15.639 --> 00:02:18.280
So this is purely when we are the server.

52
00:02:19.159 --> 00:02:21.879
So we're not gonna have any local controllers.

53
00:02:21.879 --> 00:02:26.879
The only players are gonna be simulated players

54
00:02:26.960 --> 00:02:28.599
that are actually gonna be remote connections

55
00:02:28.599 --> 00:02:30.759
that are gonna be dealt with on another PC.

56
00:02:30.759 --> 00:02:33.479
So we are responsible for sending data to them,

57
00:02:33.479 --> 00:02:36.400
but us ourselves, well, we are the server,

58
00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:38.919
so we're the thing responsible for managing

59
00:02:38.919 --> 00:02:41.159
all the authoritative state about the game.

60
00:02:41.159 --> 00:02:43.639
But also, we know we're not gonna be displaying

61
00:02:43.639 --> 00:02:44.479
any visuals.

62
00:02:44.479 --> 00:02:46.319
We know we don't need to be displaying effects

63
00:02:46.319 --> 00:02:49.169
or playing sound effects or anything like that.

64
00:02:49.169 --> 00:02:50.210
Then we've got listen server.

65
00:02:50.210 --> 00:02:51.449
Again, we've talked about the role

66
00:02:51.449 --> 00:02:53.849
of the listen server already,

67
00:02:53.849 --> 00:02:58.849
but in this context, we are both a server and a client.

68
00:02:58.849 --> 00:03:00.610
So this net mode listen server

69
00:03:00.610 --> 00:03:02.490
is only gonna be true for the person

70
00:03:02.490 --> 00:03:04.409
who is the listen server.

71
00:03:04.409 --> 00:03:06.610
Everyone else is gonna be a client.

72
00:03:06.610 --> 00:03:10.610
So if I am hosting an online co-op game

73
00:03:13.370 --> 00:03:17.530
and I am the host and I'm hosting the server locally,

74
00:03:17.530 --> 00:03:20.129
then it's quite likely I would be a listen server then

75
00:03:20.129 --> 00:03:22.530
and that means I am both a client playing

76
00:03:22.530 --> 00:03:24.610
and I am a server responsible for sending

77
00:03:24.610 --> 00:03:26.969
all the information of my local machine

78
00:03:26.969 --> 00:03:29.729
out to other connected clients.

79
00:03:29.729 --> 00:03:31.770
So that's that situation.

80
00:03:31.770 --> 00:03:33.889
And then last of all, we have client,

81
00:03:33.889 --> 00:03:36.490
which is kind of the opposite of dedicated server

82
00:03:36.490 --> 00:03:40.849
where we're kind of expecting to be not the authority

83
00:03:40.849 --> 00:03:43.409
for almost any data in the game

84
00:03:43.409 --> 00:03:46.490
or most of the authoritative data about the game

85
00:03:46.490 --> 00:03:47.689
is gonna be coming into us.

86
00:03:47.689 --> 00:03:50.050
We're not gonna be sending a huge amount out.

87
00:03:50.129 --> 00:03:53.009
It is our responsibility to send particular updates

88
00:03:53.009 --> 00:03:54.370
to the server.

89
00:03:54.370 --> 00:03:57.770
So things like input or state changes

90
00:03:57.770 --> 00:03:59.770
that we know are only local changes.

91
00:03:59.770 --> 00:04:01.129
Again, I talked about customizations

92
00:04:01.129 --> 00:04:02.729
maybe being an example of that.

93
00:04:04.099 --> 00:04:07.539
So these are things that net mode

94
00:04:07.539 --> 00:04:09.819
is something that we kind of often need to query

95
00:04:09.819 --> 00:04:13.099
about what our current context is

96
00:04:13.099 --> 00:04:15.259
and therefore what our responsibility is

97
00:04:15.259 --> 00:04:16.740
for kind of sending information.

98
00:04:16.740 --> 00:04:18.620
Obviously, if we are the client,

99
00:04:18.620 --> 00:04:20.579
that's the time where we might need to be calling

100
00:04:20.579 --> 00:04:24.300
server functions to send information to the server

101
00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:25.660
about our local updates.

102
00:04:25.660 --> 00:04:28.300
If we are a server, either a dedicated server

103
00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:30.899
or a listen server, then it's our kind of responsibility

104
00:04:30.899 --> 00:04:33.740
to be sending information out to other connected clients.

105
00:04:33.740 --> 00:04:35.060
If we're a listen server,

106
00:04:35.060 --> 00:04:37.420
we also know that we are gonna maintain

107
00:04:37.420 --> 00:04:39.220
a certain amount of local state

108
00:04:39.220 --> 00:04:41.379
and that's where it becomes important

109
00:04:41.379 --> 00:04:43.180
to kind of bear in mind things like

110
00:04:43.180 --> 00:04:47.139
not necessarily trusting your replicated using functions

111
00:04:47.139 --> 00:04:49.500
to get called because it's not actually

112
00:04:49.500 --> 00:04:52.259
gonna get replicated because it's local.

113
00:04:52.259 --> 00:04:53.579
So all of these things, you know,

114
00:04:53.579 --> 00:04:55.620
these things all have various meanings

115
00:04:55.620 --> 00:04:58.910
and permutations in different scenarios.

116
00:04:58.910 --> 00:05:01.149
Next, we have net role

117
00:05:01.149 --> 00:05:04.470
and this can easily be confused with net mode

118
00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:05.870
but it's important to talk about,

119
00:05:05.870 --> 00:05:08.509
it's actually, these are two quite distinct

120
00:05:08.509 --> 00:05:10.110
and importantly distinct things.

121
00:05:10.110 --> 00:05:12.910
So you can't, these two things are not interchangeable.

122
00:05:12.910 --> 00:05:14.790
Net role is essentially to describe

123
00:05:14.790 --> 00:05:19.399
who has authority over a given entity.

124
00:05:19.399 --> 00:05:21.920
So the three situations that you can have

125
00:05:21.920 --> 00:05:26.040
are role authority, role simulated proxy

126
00:05:26.040 --> 00:05:28.319
or role autonomous proxy.

127
00:05:28.319 --> 00:05:31.639
Authority lets us know essentially whether,

128
00:05:33.480 --> 00:05:37.439
who basically controls the data about this actor, right?

129
00:05:38.319 --> 00:05:43.319
So if we go for role authority,

130
00:05:44.199 --> 00:05:46.079
this is typically gonna be the case

131
00:05:46.079 --> 00:05:48.160
for most things on the server.

132
00:05:48.160 --> 00:05:52.279
The server has authority over the vast majority

133
00:05:52.279 --> 00:05:55.240
of the kind of game data

134
00:05:55.240 --> 00:05:57.279
but in the situation of like,

135
00:05:58.480 --> 00:06:00.839
we go to play an attack animation

136
00:06:00.839 --> 00:06:02.839
and we hit against a wall, right?

137
00:06:02.839 --> 00:06:05.600
Then we might spawn some visual effect actors,

138
00:06:05.600 --> 00:06:07.519
we might spawn some sound effects.

139
00:06:07.519 --> 00:06:09.399
It is not, the server doesn't need to know

140
00:06:09.399 --> 00:06:10.240
about those things, right?

141
00:06:10.240 --> 00:06:12.720
We are going to spawn those sound effects

142
00:06:12.759 --> 00:06:17.759
and those visual effects locally to our player.

143
00:06:19.279 --> 00:06:20.920
The server doesn't need to care about them

144
00:06:20.920 --> 00:06:23.920
and therefore those actors are our responsibility.

145
00:06:23.920 --> 00:06:25.560
We are full control over them.

146
00:06:25.560 --> 00:06:27.839
We will have a unique copy of those things.

147
00:06:27.839 --> 00:06:32.079
It literally doesn't matter if we're client A,

148
00:06:32.079 --> 00:06:34.839
it doesn't matter if client B never knows about them,

149
00:06:34.839 --> 00:06:36.240
it's kind of their responsibility

150
00:06:36.240 --> 00:06:38.399
to spawn their own visuals and sound effects

151
00:06:38.399 --> 00:06:39.560
if they need them

152
00:06:39.560 --> 00:06:41.399
but we've just kind of done this locally.

153
00:06:41.439 --> 00:06:44.680
In that situation, the remote client

154
00:06:44.680 --> 00:06:47.560
would have the authority over those sound effects,

155
00:06:47.560 --> 00:06:50.879
over those locally spawned,

156
00:06:52.470 --> 00:06:54.470
over the sound effects or the visual effects.

157
00:06:54.470 --> 00:06:58.149
You would also be the authority for any of your UI

158
00:06:58.149 --> 00:07:00.750
because again, this is not being controlled by the server.

159
00:07:00.750 --> 00:07:03.949
You as the local player, as a local connected client

160
00:07:03.949 --> 00:07:06.629
are the authority over any changes

161
00:07:06.629 --> 00:07:07.589
that are happening to that data

162
00:07:07.589 --> 00:07:09.589
are something that you as the local computer

163
00:07:09.589 --> 00:07:10.629
are in control of.

164
00:07:12.230 --> 00:07:15.350
The other situation obviously is that we are the server

165
00:07:15.350 --> 00:07:17.389
in which case we are the authority

166
00:07:17.389 --> 00:07:19.629
for the vast majority of the data,

167
00:07:19.629 --> 00:07:21.589
in which case it's our responsibility

168
00:07:21.589 --> 00:07:25.110
to replicate data to other things.

169
00:07:25.110 --> 00:07:26.430
If we are in control of that data,

170
00:07:26.430 --> 00:07:28.149
we need to send that data out

171
00:07:28.149 --> 00:07:30.589
to all the kind of simulated entities.

172
00:07:30.589 --> 00:07:35.029
Again, obviously authority, when we are a listen server,

173
00:07:35.949 --> 00:07:37.790
we have authority over both of those things.

174
00:07:37.790 --> 00:07:40.230
We have authority over our local UI,

175
00:07:40.230 --> 00:07:44.269
over our locally spawned visual effects and sound effects.

176
00:07:44.269 --> 00:07:47.389
And we also have authority over the positions

177
00:07:47.389 --> 00:07:50.870
of all the enemies because we are also the server.

178
00:07:50.870 --> 00:07:52.430
So again, that's why these two things

179
00:07:52.430 --> 00:07:53.509
don't necessarily line up

180
00:07:53.509 --> 00:07:56.490
because they are different in different scenarios.

181
00:07:57.649 --> 00:08:00.930
Simulated proxy is when an actor

182
00:08:00.930 --> 00:08:02.610
is kind of spawned on the server

183
00:08:02.610 --> 00:08:04.769
and replicated down to the local client,

184
00:08:04.769 --> 00:08:06.930
but it is owned by another client.

185
00:08:06.930 --> 00:08:10.889
So this is gonna be something like

186
00:08:10.889 --> 00:08:12.610
the enemy players in your game,

187
00:08:12.610 --> 00:08:14.009
they are gonna be simulated proxy.

188
00:08:14.009 --> 00:08:15.170
So all you're receiving

189
00:08:15.170 --> 00:08:18.009
is a simulated representation of that thing.

190
00:08:18.009 --> 00:08:20.769
The server is controlling it.

191
00:08:20.769 --> 00:08:23.089
The server might be getting information about it

192
00:08:23.089 --> 00:08:24.329
from a different client,

193
00:08:24.329 --> 00:08:26.089
but ultimately all you need to know

194
00:08:26.089 --> 00:08:28.329
is this is being controlled from elsewhere.

195
00:08:28.329 --> 00:08:31.209
You do not have control over it.

196
00:08:31.209 --> 00:08:32.769
You do not have responsibility for it.

197
00:08:32.769 --> 00:08:34.450
You're just getting all this information

198
00:08:34.450 --> 00:08:36.720
essentially from the server.

199
00:08:36.720 --> 00:08:40.080
And then last of all, we have autonomous proxy.

200
00:08:40.080 --> 00:08:43.080
Autonomous proxy is when it's spawned on the server,

201
00:08:43.080 --> 00:08:45.080
but it's kind of the local machine

202
00:08:45.080 --> 00:08:49.240
that is kind of has a degree of control over it.

203
00:08:49.240 --> 00:08:51.720
So this is gonna be your local player controller,

204
00:08:51.720 --> 00:08:54.679
your pawn.

205
00:08:54.679 --> 00:08:57.240
These are gonna be autonomous proxies.

206
00:08:57.240 --> 00:09:01.200
So it's the server that actually has control over the data

207
00:09:01.200 --> 00:09:03.759
but you have a degree of responsibility

208
00:09:03.759 --> 00:09:05.440
for kind of making changes about it

209
00:09:05.440 --> 00:09:07.720
and sending those things to the server to say,

210
00:09:07.720 --> 00:09:11.200
hey server, you know, I've updated my position.

211
00:09:11.200 --> 00:09:13.720
And so, you know, please be notified of that.

212
00:09:13.720 --> 00:09:16.399
The server may make corrections and things like that,

213
00:09:16.399 --> 00:09:19.320
but yeah, autonomous proxy is going to describe

214
00:09:19.320 --> 00:09:20.960
your role as a player

215
00:09:20.960 --> 00:09:24.039
for the things that you are kind of player controlling.
